{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"752e0d0c10df0028","x":-240,"y":-880,"width":500,"height":420,"type":"text","text":"## Macro Economics\n\nStudy of the economy as a whole, considers the effects of:\n\n* Inflation\n* Economic growth\n* Unemployment\n* Interest rates\n* Exchange rates\n\nCan effect considerations of investment firms\n\n* Some investments benefit from **slow economic growth** and low inflation\n* Some benefit from **fast growth** and moderate inflation\n* Determines which asset classes to invest in"},
		{"id":"0edc11eac22c6257","x":-960,"y":-1240,"width":600,"height":440,"type":"text","text":"## GDP and Business Cycles\n\nGDP: **Gross domestic product** is the **total value** of all final **products** and **services** produced in a **country** over a **period of time**.\n\n*note: GDP is calculated by recording when money is spent to purchase final product or service, so its basically the total money spent in a country*\n\nGDI: Total **economic output** from **income side**; **aggregate income** earned by all **households**, **businesses** and **government** entities in a **country** over given **period of time**.\n\n*note: exports are captured smoothly by GDI because when foreign customers purchase exports the revenue flows into the domestic economy*\n\n![[Pasted image 20260924173126.png|301]]\n\n### GDP Calculations\n\n#### Income approach\n\nGross domestic income (GDI) should == GDP\n\n![[Pasted image 20260924182655.png|322]]\n\n\n#### Expenditure approach\n\n**GDP = C + I + G + (X-M)**\n\n* Consumer (household spending): **C**\n* Business spending (gross investment): **I**\n* Government spending: **G**\n* Exports (foreign spending on domestic products/services): **X**\n* Imports(domestic spending on foreign products/services): **M**\n\n\n\n\n"}
	],
